(4725, 'HEY! HEY YOU! $R! Get me out of here!', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4726, '%s groans.', '', 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4727, 'Ok, let''s take a look at this thing...', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4728, 'Oh, darn...', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4729, '', 'Ok!  Let''s get started!', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4730, '', '... oops.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4731, 'Get it over with you filthy $r.$B$B<Kharan lowers his head, exposing his stubby neck.>', '', 0, 0, 0, 16, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4732, 'I am not here to harm you, Kharan. Gor''shak sent me. He told me that you would speak to me about the Princess.', 'I am not here to harm you, Kharan. Gor''shak sent me. He told me that you would speak to me about the Princess.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4733, 'All is lost...', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4734, 'All is not lost, Kharan!', 'All is not lost, Kharan!', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4735, 'Do I look stupid to you, $r? I may as well sign her death warrant myself! Why should I trust you?
', '', 0, 0, 0, 26, 5, 6, 0, 0, 0),
(4736, 'Because you are still alive and my hands aren''t gripped firmly around your stubby little neck.', 'Because you are still alive and my hands aren''t gripped firmly around your stubby little neck.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4737, '<Kharan sighs.>$B$BI suppose... I suppose you are right.$B$BGor''shak told me that your Warchief has big plans. Plans that may change the way the Alliance and Horde interact. What do you know about this?', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 6, 0, 0, 0),
(4738, 'Nothing. My orders were to speak with you and then speak with Thrall. All I know is that Thrall is interested in saving your princess.
', 'Nothing. My orders were to speak with you and then speak with Thrall. All I know is that Thrall is interested in saving your princess.
', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4739, 'Then listen well, $r.$B$BSeveral months ago, the Magistrate of Lakeshire sent envoys to Ironforge, pleading with the King for assistance with the Blackrock incursions coming from Redridge and the Burning Steppes.$B$BPrincess Moira volunteered to help, against my pleadings. I was assigned twenty elite guardsmen to protect the Princess through the perilous journey from the Loch to Lakeshire.', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(4740, 'Which would explain why you''re sitting in a jail cell at the bottom of a mountain, right, dwarf?', 'Which would explain why you''re sitting in a jail cell at the bottom of a mountain, right, dwarf?', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4741, '<Kharan clears his throat.>$B$BWe made our way through the Searing Gorge tunnel and into the ravaged wasteland comprising the gorge. In retrospect, things were eerily quiet. The only dangers we ran across were the wildlife of the region: Creatures that my men easily dispatched.$B$BWe reached Blackrock Mountain with relative ease and made our way through the stonewrought construction without so much as a hiccup.', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(4742, 'So what happened?', 'So what happened?', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4743, 'As we were making our way across the Burning Steppes, we were ambushed. It must have been a hundred of them... Dark Iron dwarves! They were shifting out of the walls, from the rocks in the Steppes; out of every crevice, nook, and cranny in sight. They swarmed us, overwhelming the guards and the few brave heroes that had agreed to assist us on this mission.$B$BOne thing was clear: This was a highly orchestrated ambush. It was as if they knew every move we would make before we made them...', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(4744, 'So you suspect that someone on the inside was involved? They were tipped off?', 'So you suspect that someone on the inside was involved? They were tipped off?', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4745, 'How else could this have happened? Someone must have tipped the Dark Irons off.$B$B<Kharan shakes his fist at you.>$B$BSo help me, if I ever get out of here, I will spend the rest of my days finding the traitor.', '', 0, 0, 0, 6, 15, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(4746, 'Continue with your story please.', 'Continue with your story please.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4747, 'Where was I? Oh yes, so we were captured. My elite guardsmen were executed on the spot. They spared me and took the princess away by way of ram. I was taken to the detention halls of the Slag Pit and then transferred to this prison.$B$BI can only assume I am still alive because they wish to extract a ransom for my pitiful life. Or maybe out of cruelty, as a way to let me forever play back the events that transpired in my mind. Regret is the cruelest jailor of all, $r.', '', 0, 0, 0, 6, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(4748, 'Indeed.', 'Indeed.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4749, 'She now resides at the side of Emperor Thaurissan. He has her under some sort of powerful thought altering spell... and here I sit, completely helpless.
', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4750, 'If it''s any consolation, I''ll be leaving the cell door open. How you get out is your problem. Good bye, Kharan. 
', 'If it''s any consolation, I''ll be leaving the cell door open. How you get out is your problem. Good bye, Kharan. 
', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4751, '', '%s holds the Rune of Escape in front of her.', 2, 0, 0, 193, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4752, 'I am here!', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;



', 'My apologies, Lady Prestor.
', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4994, '', 'You seek to lower our global defenses in order to appease a paranoid magistrate and an encampment of riff-raff that are most probably suffering from heat stroke.', 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(4995, 'Begging your pardon, Lady Prestor. That was not my intent.
', 'Begging your pardon, Lady Prestor. That was not my intent.
', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4996, '', 'Of course not, dear $g boy:girl;. You ''adventurer'' types are often victims of circumstance; subject to the political drama which tends to unfold between citizenry and royalty.$B$BMy advice to you, then, is to seek out something else, more specifically: A new career.$B$BThis world has enough heroes.', 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(4997, 'Thank you for your time, Lady Prestor.', 'Thank you for your time, Lady Prestor.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4998, '%s gets really dizzy!', '', 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(4999, '%s drunkenly miscasts a shadow bolt!', '%s drunkenly miscasts a shadow bolt!', 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5000, '', 'Hey, Rocknot!', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5001, '', 'Let''s go, honey.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5002, '', '%s kisses her lover.', 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5003, '%s kisses Mistress Nagmara', '', 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5004, 'Please, help me to get through this cursed forest, $r.', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5005, 'The corruption of the fel has not left any of the creatures of Felwood untouched, $n. Please, be on your guard.', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5006, 'What you be wanting? *hic*', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5007, 'Official business, John. I need some information about Marshal Windsor. Tell me about the last time you saw him.', 'Official business, John. I need some information about Marshal Windsor. Tell me about the last time you saw him.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5008, 'That I must fight against my own kind deeply saddens me.', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5009, 'Windsor was particularly ornery that day - and believe me, for Windsor, that''s a monumental accomplishment. He kept telling me that ''something feels off.'' Well he wasn''t kidding!$B$BWe were in the middle of Blackrock Mountain when the filthy animals attacked. I''m talking about the orcs, of course. Pay attention, will ya? All you could hear were grunts and the clanging of steel as they rushed us. ', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 6, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(5010, 'So what did you do?', 'So what did you do?', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5012, 'Me versus fifty orcs? I''m no fool, $n. My pappy always told me, ''Discreditin is the better part of a cracker,'' or something, and I knew what that meant.', '', 0, 0, 0, 6, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5013, 'Start making sense, dwarf. I don''t want to have anything to do with your cracker, your pappy, or any sort of ''discreditin.''
', 'Start making sense, dwarf. I don''t want to have anything to do with your cracker, your pappy, or any sort of ''discreditin.''
', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5014, 'Alright, alright. Anyhow, so I sorta slipped into the shadows.$B$BThat didn''t sit too well with Windsor, seeing as how he was already extra cranky. Well he started spinnin'' old Ironfoe around and screaming like a mad man at the orcs. ', '', 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(5015, 'Ironfoe?
', 'Ironfoe?
', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5016, 'Yep. You never heard of Ironfoe? The legendary orc slaying hammer? Yep, yep, that was ol'' Windsor''s hammer. He told me that Franclorn Forgewright himself made that hammer for his great, great, grand pappy. THE Franclorn Forgewright: The Dark Iron responsible for stonewrought archimetenc... building stuff. He also said the hammer had a twin that Franclorn kept for himself. Think he called it Ironfel or something.', '', 0, 0, 0, 6, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(5017, 'Interesting... continue, John.', 'Interesting... continue, John.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5018, 'So where was I? Oh yea, so the orcs rushed Windsor and Windsor, well, he didn''t move an inch. He stood tall as they charged him, ten at a time. All I could see was the glow from Ironfoe and a lot of blood. This went on for hours, maybe days. I don''t remember. Anyhow, FINALLY, it stopped.', '', 0, 0, 0, 6, 5, 5, 0, 0, 0),
(5019, 'So that''s how Windsor died...', 'So that''s how Windsor died...', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5020, 'Died? Are you cracked, $n? Excuse me, $g Mister:Miss; $n! Windsor wouldn''t have died from no fifty orcs. As sure as Thelsamar blood sausage is the tastiest food the world may ever know, there he stood: He was covered in orc chunks from head to toe, drenched in about eighteen layers of their blood, but he was definitely alive... and really, really angry.', '', 0, 0, 0, 6, 6, 5, 0, 0, 0),
(5021, 'So how did he die?', 'So how did he die?', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5022, 'Why do you keep saying he died? Who told you he died? I never said he died.$B$BHe went missing is all.$B$BYou see, apparently we had gotten into the middle of some big orc versus Dark Iron dwarf battle. The orcs, being the filthy, miserable curs that they are, were out early, setting up some traps and other diabolical things you probably wouldn''t understand.', '', 0, 0, 0, 6, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(5023, 'I can sense it now, $n. Ashenvale lies down this path.', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5024, 'Ok, so where the hell is he? Wait a minute! Are you drunk?', 'Ok, so where the hell is he? Wait a minute! Are you drunk?', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5025, 'Dwarves don''t get drunk, $g mister:missy;. I''m just a little sloppy.$B$BAnyhow, Windsor? I figure he''s somewhere in Blackrock Depths. That''s the Dark Iron city for you unedumecated peoples.', '', 0, 0, 0, 14, 6, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(5026, 'I feel... something strange...', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5027, 'WHY is he in Blackrock Depths?', 'WHY is he in Blackrock Depths?', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5028, 'Slow down! I was getting to that!$B$BSo there he was, standing tall with all the blood and guts dripping off him when who shows up?$B$BThe Dark Irons! Didn''t you hear a word I said??$B$BWell, the Dark Irons are a little craftier than those Blackrock orcs. They came prepared. By prepared I mean there were about 300 of em... *hic* ''scuse me.', '', 0, 0, 0, 5, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(5029, '$n, my form has now changed! The true strength of my spirit is returning to me now... The cursed grasp of the forest is leaving me.', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5030, '300? So the Dark Irons killed him and dragged him into the Depths?', '300? So the Dark Irons killed him and dragged him into the Depths?', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5031, '$G Mister:Missy;, if I didn''t know better, I''d think you were one of them ''special'' peoples. We call em Troggs.$B$BWindsor didn''t have no beef with the Dark Irons, after all, his great, great, grand pappy''s best friend was a Dark Iron. Which is also probably why that army of Dark Irons didn''t kill him on sight.', '', 0, 0, 0, 25, 1, 5, 0, 0, 0),
(5032, 'Your knowledge is lacking.  Return to me when your skills in smelting have grown!', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5033, 'You may leave me here -- I wish to be alone in my final moments.', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5034, 'Ahhh... Ironfoe.
', 'Ahhh... Ironfoe.
', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5035, 'Finally! Put some fingers in your ears, your brain mighta just grown five sizes and I''m worried it might leak out.$B$BSo, the Dark Irons spared his life and took him prisoner. Their leader, some self-important, uppity fella named Thauris-something, took Ironfoe for himself. And that was the last I saw of ol'' Windsor... *hic* ''scuse me.
', '', 0, 0, 0, 5, 1, 33, 0, 0, 0),
(5036, 'Thank you, $n. Now my spirit will finally be at peace.', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5037, 'The corruption of Felwood has trapped my spirit here... I may never rest...', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5038, 'Thanks, Ragged John. Your story was very uplifting and informative. ', 'Thanks, Ragged John. Your story was very uplifting and informative. ', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5039, '', 'Welcome to the Grim Guzzler!', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5040, 'Why don''t you and Rocknot go find somewhere private...', 'Why don''t you and Rocknot go find somewhere private...', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5041, '', 'Good idea!', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5042, '', 'Thanks again, $n.  Rocknot and I are really hitting it off!', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5043, 'Another Engineer! Hey, this is a great chance for me to show off some new gadgets I''ve been building!', 'Another Engineer! Hey, this is a great chance for me to show off some new gadgets I''ve been building!', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5044, '', 'If you''re going to venture into Blackrock Depths, come speak with me. I may have some work for you.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5045, '%s looks tired. He then yawns and lies down next to A-Me 01', '', 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5046, '%s snores loudly and cuddles up next to A-Me 01.', '', 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5047, '', 'Have you seen all the wonderful things here in Ungoro Crater, $n? It''s simply amazing. Not as amazing as some of the things I can make with my skill at engineering, but for it being all natural here... it''s not too bad.$B$BMy uncle Remtravel loves old stuff like this place. I''m following in his footsteps kinda--I want to discover new things from lost cultures too!', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5048, '', 'Hmm, I don''t have any mithril casings. I''m all out. Is that all you need to get to fix A-Me? Oh, that would be fantastic!$B$BMithril casings aren''t too hard to find back in civilization. Just ask any skilled engineer to make one for you. I think it takes a few bars of mithril, but if you could help me out, I''ll make sure you''re well rewarded!', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5049, 'Do you have any mithril casings?', 'Do you have any mithril casings?', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5050, '', 'Be sure to try our Dark Iron Ale.  I hear the dwarves around here can''t get enough of it.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5051, '', 'My master, Plugger Spazzring, is a good boss.  And he makes a lot of money.  His pockets are bursting!', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(5052, 'This here is the finest, most state of the art mode of transportation money can build. What? Deeprun Tram? Gnomes? Listen pal, If you believe that garbage then I''ve got a statue down in Stranglethorn to sell ya. Now, are you walking to Grom''Gol or are you gonna ride in style in this fine flying machine? Your choice.', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
