(8922, 'Free! Free from my bonds at last!', '', 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8923, '$n, please take a look at the sample of the Vylestem vine that I took from the caverns, so that you know what to look for...', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8924, 'I need no home to know I still have a place in this world, $c. The tribes will see... all of them. They fight amongst one another, and for what? Scraps left over by vultures... lands infested by the Legion... bah!$B$BThe centaur should be proud of their heritage--it is just as noble as any Night elf''s or orc''s--it is time we started acting like it!', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8925, 'At last, I am free of the corruption that once bound me to this place...', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8926, 'Thank you for what you have done, $n.$B$BKeep the scepter safe; may it aid you in your toil against the evils that have invaded this place...', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8927, 'How has this come to be, $n? Do you think that an item such as the Scepter of Celebras is trivial?$B$BI can help you this time, but do not be careless with this valuable item again...', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8928, 'Celebras, I lost my Scepter...', 'Celebras, I lost my Scepter...', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8929, 'I carry both parts of the scepter.', 'I carry both parts of the scepter.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8930, 'My scepter... After so many years... You have recovered it! You shall truly be the savior of this place...$B$BPlease listen to me carefully, $n. The head and the rod of the scepter may only be reunited into one at the Stone of Maraudon.', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8931, 'Please show me the Stone of Maraudon.', 'Please show me the Stone of Maraudon.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8932, 'Please explain how the scepter works.', 'Please explain how the scepter works.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8933, 'Between the colors, a path.$B$BBlink across in light.$B$BFrom the water, you emerge.', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8934, 'I don''t quite understand...', 'I don''t quite understand...', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8935, 'Between the orange and the purple passageways near the doors to Maraudon, you will find a third path.$B$BThe scepter you hold in your hands is the key.', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8936, 'No, really, I still don''t understand...', 'No, really, I still don''t understand...', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8937, 'I grow weary...$B$BFrom here, you can see the waterfalls, $n...The scepter grants you the power to travel to this very place, should you ever desire to enter through the front gates of Maraudon again.$B$BNear the entrance to Maraudon, you will find a passage that goes down beneath the caverns. Use the scepter at the ancient ritual site to create a portal, and you will find yourself here once more.', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8938, 'Please tell me more about Maraudon.', 'Please tell me more about Maraudon.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8939, 'Long ago, my dryad sisters and I entered these caves to free the tortured spirit of my uncle, Zaetar. However, the corruption that had already spread through these caverns soon overcame us, and we too fell.$B$BWe were destined to wander these passages; the toxins poisoning our minds...$B$BAlthough my spirit may now be at rest, I know that I have failed in my mission. It is a great sadness I must bear...', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8940, 'Please tell me more about Zaetar.', 'Please tell me more about Zaetar.', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8941, 'Ah, Zaetar... <Celebras looks away.>$B$BMy father, Remulos, tried to stop him...$B$BZaetar was headstrong, and when he fell for an earthen elemental princess, my father knew that their union was cursed, but Zaetar refused to listen.$B$BThe centaur are the result of his mistake. They were born misshapen and hateful; my uncle Zaetar was killed by his own kin...$B$BThe evil princess, Theradras, still guards his remains here in the crystal caverns.', '', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8942, 'Those goblins should be ashamed of themselves.  Bah!', '', 0, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8943, 'Spending coin is NOT the reason for the Feast of Winter Veil!', '', 0, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8944, 'I cannot believe those greedy goblins are allowed to hawk their wares while spoiling the spirit of this season.', '', 0, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8945, 'Vile goblins... anything for a gold coin.', '', 0, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(8946, 'Could I have a copy of "The Feast of Winter Veil" to read?', 'Could I have a copy of "The Feast of Winter Veil" to read?', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

